1. Find no. of files present in a directory
   ls -1 | wc -l 
-1 with ls = number one.
-l with wc = lowercase letter L.
2. To combine and sort 
  cat name.txt list.txt | sort
3.To sort and get unique values
 cat name.txt | sort
 cat name.txt | sort | uniq
N.B- Before running uniq command ,data must be sorted
4. We have a 50 nos. line ,but we want only first 20 lines then
    cat file.txt | head -21 (to get first 20 lines)
    cat file.txt | tail -5 ( to get last 5 lines)
    cat file.txt | head -21 | tail -5 ( from 1 to 20 then,20 to 15 lines data)
5. netstat | more
  Useful keys:
- Space — next screen
- Enter — next line
- q — quit
6. netstat | less
  Useful keys:
- Space — next screen
- b — previous screen
- ↑ / ↓ — move up or down
- /word — search forward for a word
- n — next search match
- q — quit
7. ls | tee files.txt ( to save and show outsput in terminal)
   ls | tee files.txt | wc -l ( to count no. of files)
8. ls | echo (no output,because echo accepts only command line arguments)
   ls | xargs echo" hi"  (now it will give output with echo output)
   cat country.txt | xargs touch ( it will create files from the output of cat command)
